From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: unwind phylink on open failure

The PHY and phylink polling are started before the fallible VIP entry
setup. If it fails, ndo_open is not followed by ndo_stop. Stop queues,
stop phylink, and disconnect the PHY before returning the error.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2190,8 +2190,12 @@
 
 	netif_tx_start_all_queues(netdev);
 	err = airoha_set_vip_for_gdm_port(dev, true);
-	if (err)
+	if (err) {
+		netif_tx_disable(netdev);
+		phylink_stop(dev->phylink);
+		phylink_disconnect_phy(dev->phylink);
 		return err;
+	}
 
 	/* It seems GDM3 and GDM4 needs SPORT enabled to correctly work */
 	if (netdev_uses_dsa(netdev) || port->id > 2)
